 "body_html": "<p>I'm implementing my own malloc and free functions. How can I have an error check that passes in a static variable over a dynamically allocated variable?\nLet's say I have:</p>\n\n<pre><code>char foo[10];\nvoid *bar = malloc(5); \n\nvoid free(void *p)\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>Is there a way to tell the user that this is an error?</p>\n\n<pre><code>free(foo)\n</code></pre>\n",
 "passes": [
